        <h3>Why Worldwide Government &amp; Consular Portals Enforce Strict KB Limits</h3>
        <p>
          To understand why exact file optimization is required, consider the operational constraints of large institutional portals. When national testing agencies (like SSC, UPSC, NTA, or IBPS) or immigration authorities (such as the US Department of State CEAC portal, UK Visas &amp; Immigration UKVI, Schengen VFS Global, or Canada IRCC) open an application window, their ingest pipelines process millions of digital submissions within narrow deadlines.
        </p>
        <p>
          If each applicant uploaded uncompressed multi-megabyte photos, the intake servers would face terabytes of redundant payload transfers daily. Beyond network bandwidth, these systems run automated image recognition, biometric face-matching algorithms, and database indexing pipelines. To generate examination hall tickets, visa vignettes, and security dossiers efficiently, intake systems enforce strict limits on file weight (e.g., 20KB to 50KB or under 240KB) and resolution density (200 or 300 DPI).
        </p>

